.TH TERMNAV-SWITCH-TAB 1 "2026-07-29" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
termnav-switch-tab \- switch the nearest parent terminal tab scope
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termnav-switch-tab
.RI [ next | previous ]
.B \-\-client\-pid
.I PID
.B \-\-client\-tty
.I TTY
.B \-\-client\-termtype
.I TYPE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B termnav-switch-tab
routes a tab switch outward from a one-window tmux session. It walks locally
nested tmux clients first and switches the first parent session with multiple
windows. If no parent tmux owns the request, it delegates to the outer VS Code
window or WezTerm client.
.PP
The tmux binding supplies client identity explicitly so sessions attached from
multiple terminal windows do not share stale process-global routing state.
.PP
For each local parent, only a client whose active pane matches the child tmux
pane is eligible. The newest client activity wins. A unique focused client
breaks an activity tie; any remaining ambiguity fails closed.
.PP
At a VS Code boundary, the helper uses only the socket published in the
triggering client's environment. It never uses an inherited process-global
socket, telemetry identity, or product CLI hook. Terminals already open when
the adapter is installed must be relaunched once to receive the socket
variable. First install also requires reloading the editor window so it
discovers the adapter. Because every adapter activation claims a fresh socket,
terminal or tmux clients must also be relaunched after an extension-host or
editor-window restart; stale clients fail closed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B next
Switch to the next tab or window. This is the default.
.TP
.B previous
Switch to the previous tab or window.
.TP
.BI \-\-client\-pid " PID"
PID of the tmux client that received the key.
.TP
.BI \-\-client\-tty " TTY"
Terminal device of the tmux client.
.TP
.BI \-\-client\-termtype " TYPE"
Terminal type reported by tmux for the client.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_FALLBACK_BACKEND
Optional backend used only when the triggering VS Code client has no published
socket. Unset by default so ambiguous VS Code routing fails closed. Set to
.B mcp
only when process-global routing is acceptable.
.TP
.B TERMNAV_VSCODE_SOCKET
Read from the triggering tmux client process, not from this helper's inherited
environment.
.SH LIMITATIONS
An ordinary SSH or mosh hop cannot carry the WezTerm output-side parent
loopback into VS Code. A one-window remote tmux inside VS Code therefore needs
an explicitly configured reverse bridge or the request fails closed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vscode-switch-tab (1),
.BR wezterm-switch-tab (1)
